{"base_rate":0.43783783783783786,"brier":0.1680327027027027,"bss":0.3173172780151947,"bss_hi":0.4154254689541281,"bss_lo":0.20352434577692238,"country":"AU","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.12270270270270271,"ess":359.57950922482723,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Sydney</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Sydney rain forecast is moderately skilful, though 5 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (99%), believe about\n<b>85%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>10%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 740 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nSYDNEY BOTANIC GARDENS, 0.8 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.32, ranked 55 of\n109 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(31&ndash;89) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>10%</b></td><td class='num'>206</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>9%</td><td class='num'><b>17%</b></td><td class='num'>83</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>30%</td><td class='num'><b>33%</b></td><td class='num'>78</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>59%</td><td class='num'><b>44%</b></td><td class='num'>72</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>82%</td><td class='num'><b>53%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>99%</td><td class='num'><b>85%</b></td><td class='num'>225</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">5 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Sydney</b> <span class=\"muted\">AU</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag ok\">Moderately skilful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">5 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.32</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>31&ndash;89\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 109</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>740 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Sydney &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Sydney\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"59.546601941747575,376.6990291262136 89.0922891566265,329.3734939759036 164.8807692307692,232.66666666666669 266.81083333333333,124.16666666666663 347.4881578947369,56.31578947368422 407.15413333333333,18.0 407.15413333333333,29.324444444444453 347.4881578947369,113.78947368421052 266.81083333333333,210.11111111111111 164.8807692307692,307.33333333333337 89.0922891566265,368.8433734939759 59.546601941747575,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"222.62702702702703\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"222.62702702702703\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"59.546601941747575,346.6601941747573 89.0922891566265,320.6024096385542 164.8807692307692,260.6666666666667 266.81083333333333,220.22222222222223 347.4881578947369,190.42105263157896 407.15413333333333,71.38666666666666\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 10% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 206 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"59.546601941747575\" cy=\"346.6601941747573\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 9%&amp;#10;It rained 17% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 83 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"89.0922891566265\" cy=\"320.6024096385542\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 30%&amp;#10;It rained 33% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 78 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"164.8807692307692\" cy=\"260.6666666666667\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 59%&amp;#10;It rained 44% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 72 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"266.81083333333333\" cy=\"220.22222222222223\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 82%&amp;#10;It rained 53% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 76 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"347.4881578947369\" cy=\"190.42105263157896\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 99%&amp;#10;It rained 85% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 225 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"407.15413333333333\" cy=\"71.38666666666666\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(44%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Sydney the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (0.42) and least in\n<b>winter</b> (0.04).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>158</td><td class='num'>41%</td><td class='num'>0.041</td><td class='num'>18.2%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>33%</td><td class='num'>0.315</td><td class='num'>12.4%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>44%</td><td class='num'>0.365</td><td class='num'>10.0%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>218</td><td class='num'>54%</td><td class='num'>0.419</td><td class='num'>8.1%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":-33.86785,"lon":151.20732,"n":740,"n_cities":109,"name":"Sydney","offset_days":-1,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.04,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0043689320388349525,"n":206,"obs":0.0970873786407767,"sig":true},{"hi":0.18,"lo":0.04,"mean":0.08783132530120481,"n":83,"obs":0.1686746987951807,"sig":true},{"hi":0.47,"lo":0.18,"mean":0.3019230769230769,"n":78,"obs":0.3333333333333333,"sig":false},{"hi":0.73,"lo":0.47,"mean":0.5898611111111111,"n":72,"obs":0.4444444444444444,"sig":true},{"hi":0.92,"lo":0.73,"mean":0.817763157894737,"n":76,"obs":0.5263157894736842,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.92,"mean":0.98631111111111